  "passage": "Last week, our school held its annual Career Day in the main hall. Students from all years gathered to learn about different occupations. One of the most exciting talks was by Mr. Davies, a former astronaut. He described what it's like to travel in a spaceship and see Earth from above. Many students were inspired, but some disagreed about whether space travel is important. During the session, we sat in a circle beside the stage to ask questions. I realised that being an astronaut requires a lot of hard work and training. The event was part of our school's eightieth anniversary celebrations, which have been happening all season. Mr. Davies showed photos from his missions and talked about the beauty of seeing the planet from space. He encouraged us to pursue our dreams. After the talk, we had a workshop where we discussed our favourite occupations in small groups. It was a memorable day for everyone.",
